e can win it. Marie Gluesenkamp Perez has outraised John Braun by roughly three to one and holds a cash advantage, and betting markets put her chances near ninety percent. Expert raters mostly call the race Likely or Lean Democratic, though Cook and Inside Elections see a true toss-up.\n\nThe polling record is thin and dated, and the race has drawn national attention as a potential House majority decider, including a Trump-backed PAC entering the fray. A liberal primary rival has declined to endorse the incumbent, adding a small complication. The evidence still favors Perez, but with enough uncertainty that a six-point margin carries real risk of a much closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8833, "margin": 7.32}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8392, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8323, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8357, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8044, "margin": 6.0}]}